  "Question": "A man has \\(\\$2.73\\) in pennies, nickels, dimes, quarters and half dollars. If he has an equal number of coins of each kind, then the total number of coins he has is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(5\\)",
    "C": "\\(9\\)",
    "D": "\\(10\\)",
    "E": "\\(15\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Because there are equally many coins of each kind, we can group all the coins into sets containing one penny, one nickel, one dime, one quarter, and one half dollar. Each set contains five coins and is worth\n\\[\n1+5+10+25+50=91\\text{ cents}.\n\\]\nThe total is \\(273\\) cents, so the number of sets is\n\\[\n273\\div91=3.\n\\]\nThus there are \\(3\\times5=15\\) coins, choice E.",
